  {
   "approach": "Start at the end of the park road at the Bugaboo Creek trailhead and take the Conrad Kain Hut trail, about 5 km one way with roughly 700 m of gain, steep and with chained sections near the top. Climbers camp at the hut or at the Applebee Dome campground on the rock slab above it. From the Applebee campground the line sits toward the right of the wall: broken ledges rise off the glacier to a corner system that angles up and right. descend to the glacier below the wall and walk to the base, stepping across the moat at the rock, which gets harder as summer goes on. Bring an axe and rope for the glacier.",
